    <briefdescription>
<para>NUMA-aware memory allocator (v1.9.0, Issue #228). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Optimises memory allocation and data placement for NUMA architectures by:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Detecting the system NUMA topology on construction.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Allocating memory on the calling thread&apos;s local node when possible.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Supporting explicit node placement for performance-critical structures.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Providing a migration helper to move allocations to a preferred node.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Falling back transparently to standard malloc/free when NUMA primitives are unavailable (containers, non-Linux).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Research basis: &quot;NUMA-aware Memory Management&quot; (ASPLOS&apos;15).</para>
<para>Performance targets:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Local access ratio &gt; 90 %</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Remote access penalty: -60 % vs unoptimised allocation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Throughput: +30-80 % on NUMA systems vs single-node allocation</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>Thread safety: all public methods are thread-safe. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
